   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Comparar dos cosas",
    "@en": "Compare two things"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "Para comparar dos cosas, muchos adjetivos cortos añaden **-er**: **cheap → cheaper**, **small → smaller**. En algunos se dobla la consonante final: **big → bigger**.",
     "@en": "To compare two things, many short adjectives add **-er**: **cheap → cheaper**, **small → smaller**. In some, the final consonant is doubled: **big → bigger**."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Con adjetivos largos usamos **more**: **more expensive**. Después de un comparativo podemos usar **than** («que»): **This phone is cheaper than that phone**.",
     "@en": "With long adjectives we use **more**: **more expensive**. After a comparison we can use **than** («that»): **This phone is cheaper than that phone**."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Una forma frecuente e irregular es **good → better** (bueno → mejor). En A2 se ampliarán las reglas y otras formas.",
     "@en": "A frequent and irregular form is **good → better** (good → better). In A2 the rules and other forms will be extended."
    }
   ]
